 "summary": "The ordered region, its Fubini splitting, and the identification with `orderedProdIntegral` have no counterpart in Mathlib (no measurable-set-of-strictly-monotone lemma, no simplex volume, and `Integral/Pi.lean` covers only product integrands over the full pi space), and the proofs reuse `volume_preserving_piFinSuccAbove`, `Fin.strictMono_cons`, `MeasurableSet.univ_pi'`, `Set.ofPred_forall` and `integral_prod` rather than re-deriving them. Downstream results chain through `orderedProdIntegral_eq` and the `f = 1` instance instead of repeating the induction.",
